## When to use a PEM

The piecewise exponential model is a good choice when:

- You want an explicit baseline hazard estimate (for reporting rates, not just relative effects).
- The hazard has clear period structure (early mortality, treatment plateau, late relapse).
- You need to extrapolate beyond observed follow-up but do not want to commit to a parametric
distribution shape.
- You are bridging between a nonparametric analysis and a fully parametric one and want to check
sensitivity to baseline hazard assumptions.
